 "summary": {
  "v2_E0038": "7 of 7 conditions ended at the 0.25 h CPU cap inside a slow stretch, after 0, 1, 2, 2, 4, 4 and 20 cycles; no overlap, no audit failure, no energy gain.",
  "v3_E0039": "6 of 7 ended at the 0.5 h CPU cap after the same number of cycles as v2 (0, 1, 2, 2, 4, 20); Gamma 5 f* 0.5 depth 10 overlapped in cycle 4 (v2 reached the cap there after 4 cycles). No audit failure, no energy gain.",
  "v3_E0040": "Gamma 5 f* 0.5 depth 10 seed 2 reached the CPU cap after 2 cycles (plate-stick overlapped in zero-based cycle 2); Gamma 3.5 f* 0.3 depth 15 seed 3 overlapped in cycle 0 at phase 0.934 after a slow stretch of 100500000 events (plate-stick: cycle 0, phase 0.945).",
  "E0026_cases_passed_by_v3": "1 of 5 completes the cycle in which plate-stick failed: Gamma 5 f* 0.5 depth 10 seed 1 (plate-stick zero-based cycle 2; v3 completed 4 cycles, then overlapped). The other 4 stop in plate-stick's failure cycle: f* 0.3 depth 10 seed 1 (cycle 2, CPU cap), f* 0.3 depth 15 seed 1 (cycle 4, CPU cap), f* 0.5 depth 10 seed 2 (cycle 2, CPU cap), Gamma 3.5 f* 0.3 depth 15 seed 3 (cycle 0, overlap).",
  "diagnosis": "In all 4 stalls examined event by event (Gamma 3.5 f* 0.3 depth 15 seeds 1 and 3, Gamma 5 f* 0.5 depth 10 seed 2, Gamma 5 f* 0.3 depth 5 seed 1), one free sphere on the plate rolls without slip (horizontal speed equal to its spin surface speed: 0.0887, 0.0407, 1.06, 0.224) and takes nearly every event (tiny plate collisions and tiny collisions with one sphere pressed on it); no sphere is resting at the time. The approved rest rule needs the full speed relative to the plate below v_sleep, which a rolling sphere never has.",
  "roll_variant": "Exploratory branch method/persistent-contact-roll (c3dd7b2, plate_rest = roll): the lone rolling sphere rests and rolls on, but a 2D layer (N 150, Gamma 2.2, v_sleep 3e-2) stalls in cycle 0 at a free sphere pressed on a rolling resting sphere, which cannot be a supporter."
